  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When an electron jumps&nbsp;down from any higher energy level to the first energy level, then the emitted lines form the Lyman series</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, where<math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is the Rydberg constant.</p><p>Similarly, when an electron&nbsp;jumps down&nbsp;from any higher energy level to the second energy level, then the emitted lines form the Balmer series</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />For maximum wavelength, the energy gap should be the smallest</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
